# Don't stop here, keep learning!

## Additional Resources
* <a href="https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1WXvjG9TscUuH5Xz8Pj2okz6lMIKV__g0v6AoYVXKb40/copy " target="_blank">Large Language Model Prompts for Educators</a> from Code.org. 
* <a href="https://www.aiforeducation.io/prompt-library " target="_blank">Educator's Prompt Library</a> from AI for Education.
* <a href="https://www.teachai.org/" target="_blank">TeachAI.org</a> Empowering educators to teach with and about AI.
* <a href="https://www.teachai.org/ailiteracy" target="_blank">AILit Framework</a> from TeachAI.org.
* <a href="https://iste-ascd.org/ai" target="_blank">Artificial Intelligence in Education</a> from ISTE.

## Take it Further Activities

Want to learn more? Try out the following optional activities.
  <!-- Dropdown 1 -->
<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">

<summary style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold">
	Google AI in K12 Education
</summary>

<div style="margin-top: 10px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid #ddd;">
<p style="margin: 5px 0 10px 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;">If your school uses Google AI, take one of their online courses to learn how to make the most of those systems.
</p>

<a href="https://edu.exceedlms.com/student/path/1725537" 
         target="blank" 
         rel="noopener noreferrer" 
         style="display: inline-block; margin-top: 5px; padding: 8px 12px; background-color: #026C7A; color: #ffffff; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 14px;">Check it Out
</a>
</div>

</details>

  <!-- Dropdown 2 -->
<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">

<summary style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold">
	Tool Comparison Activity
</summary>

<div style="margin-top: 10px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid #ddd;">
<p style="margin: 5px 0 10px 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;">Every LLM responds slightly differently and users often develop preferences for one over the other. Take the time to try out the same prompt in multiple LLMs and see how the responses differ. <br><br>Reflect on which set of responses do you prefer and try to articulate why.
</p>
</div>

</details>

  <!-- Dropdown 3 -->
<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">

<summary style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold">
	In Depth Look at Prompting
</summary>

<div style="margin-top: 10px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid #ddd;">
<p style="margin: 5px 0 10px 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;">This module introduces prompting and one possible prompting framework, but prompt engineering goes way deeper. OpenAI publishes clear explanation of how prompts affect outputs and examples of improving prompts with structure and detail.
</p>

  <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/prompt-guidance" 
         target="blank" 
         rel="noopener noreferrer" 
         style="display: inline-block; margin-top: 5px; padding: 8px 12px; background-color: #026C7A; color: #ffffff; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 14px;">Check it Out
</a>
</div>

</details>

